<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
    NOTE — App Sandbox is intentionally disabled for the alpha track.

    Sparkle 2's installer flow requires `InstallerLauncher.xpc` when the
    host app is sandboxed. The Swift Package Manager distribution of
    Sparkle (`Sparkle-for-Swift-Package-Manager.zip`) does NOT include
    that helper, so a sandboxed app cannot perform auto-updates — the
    installer aborts with "An error occurred while launching the
    installer" (observed in 0.1.2-alpha).

    Alpha builds are ad-hoc signed and distributed via GitHub Releases,
    not the Mac App Store, so the sandbox brings no distribution
    requirement. Hardened Runtime stays enabled (see Project.swift) for
    notarization-readiness later. Sandbox will be re-introduced together
    with the non-SPM Sparkle distribution (which ships
    `InstallerLauncher.xpc`) once we move to Developer ID + notarization.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
